WEBVTT

00:05.580 --> 00:12.012
[Thomas Hobbes, Leviathan]

00:15.351 --> 00:18.241
Hey, did you see the new episode last night?

00:18.266 --> 00:19.917
Yeah, it was so good!

00:19.942 --> 00:22.077
What show? What's it about?

00:25.296 --> 00:28.133
I want to protect a dear friend,

00:29.047 --> 00:30.695
so I watch over the class.

00:32.418 --> 00:34.034
If I can keep the class safe,

00:34.803 --> 00:36.639
I can keep my friend safe, too.

00:38.483 --> 00:39.217
But…

00:40.374 --> 00:42.506
that's not who I really am.

00:44.319 --> 00:46.319
What happened back in middle school…

00:46.631 --> 00:48.076
I failed there.

00:49.170 --> 00:53.217
So I can't afford to repeat
the same mistake in this class.

00:54.116 --> 00:57.647
In the end, that led me to one conclusion.

00:58.045 --> 00:58.857
Namely…

01:01.147 --> 01:04.428
Horikita. Shut up for a second.

01:06.743 --> 01:08.571
Ultimately, it looks like…

01:11.041 --> 01:13.337
I failed all over again.

01:14.867 --> 01:15.934
Thanks for waiting.

01:16.610 --> 01:18.228
What did you want to discuss?

01:18.814 --> 01:20.040
Kiyotaka?

01:20.306 --> 01:24.813
If this concerns the exam, I thought it
would be best for him to be here, too.

01:24.938 --> 01:26.556
Considering he is the leader.

01:26.798 --> 01:27.821
I understand.

01:28.306 --> 01:29.173
So, what is it?

01:29.755 --> 01:33.595
I came up with a way to get
information from Class A.

01:33.978 --> 01:36.360
By following their students around?

01:36.806 --> 01:37.493
No.

01:38.978 --> 01:43.063
We can lure Katsuragi
from Class A to our side.

01:43.485 --> 01:44.626
What are you saying?

01:44.720 --> 01:47.517
Yahiko was really important to Katsuragi,

01:47.542 --> 01:51.321
so don't you think he might hold
his expulsion against Sakayanagi?

01:51.900 --> 01:55.915
He's been isolated ever since.
He doesn't fit into Class A anymore.

01:56.477 --> 01:59.574
I can't deny that he's been
at odds with Sakayanagi.

02:00.173 --> 02:05.728
But do you really think he would betray
his whole class just to get back at her?

02:06.335 --> 02:09.895
Well, the conditions would have to be just right.

02:10.334 --> 02:13.717
And do you think we can set up those conditions?

02:14.193 --> 02:19.575
If we can advance to Class A, we'll offer
to let Katsuragi transfer into our class.

02:20.121 --> 02:22.636
That would cost 20 million points.

02:22.972 --> 02:26.050
It wouldn't be impossible,
if the whole class saved up.

02:26.559 --> 02:29.886
No one in their right mind would agree to that.

02:30.215 --> 02:32.394
Besides, we're still Class C right now.

02:32.598 --> 02:37.730
If anyone were to find out, Katsuragi
would be targeted for expulsion next.

02:38.684 --> 02:42.183
We wouldn't have time to
slowly save up points before that.

02:42.692 --> 02:45.675
I'm not against fighting a war of intel.

02:46.051 --> 02:48.261
But this isn't the right strategy.

02:48.363 --> 02:51.230
If we don't do something, we won't get any intel.

02:51.676 --> 02:55.410
We won't get any by making a move
just for the sake of it, either.

02:55.816 --> 02:59.073
Come back to me if you come up
with any new ideas.

03:03.330 --> 03:05.822
Kiyotaka, would you help me with something?

03:06.174 --> 03:09.174
I already arranged to meet with Katsuragi later.

03:12.377 --> 03:15.588
What's in it for me if I do?

03:16.065 --> 03:18.065
We'd welcome you into our class.

03:18.721 --> 03:22.180
When we advance to Class A,
we'd prepare for you to transfer…

03:22.205 --> 03:23.002
Forget it.

03:24.166 --> 03:27.970
There's no way you guys can get
your hands on 20 million points.

03:29.097 --> 03:35.394
But you're not wrong that I'm still
deeply angry with Sakayanagi.

03:36.144 --> 03:40.494
Sakayanagi isn't telling anyone
which five events are real,

03:40.519 --> 03:43.985
but I don't mind telling you my guesses.

03:44.015 --> 03:47.189
Really?! But what do you want in return?

03:47.515 --> 03:51.257
All I really want is for Sakayanagi to fail.

03:52.085 --> 03:56.878
Chess, English, and math are definitely real.

03:57.066 --> 04:00.246
I'd guess modern Japanese and
mental arithmetic are, too.

04:00.801 --> 04:06.506
Group jump rope and dodgeball would require
so many people, those are most likely fake.

04:06.913 --> 04:09.637
Kiyotaka, doesn't this give us a shot at winning?

04:09.662 --> 04:13.496
No, you can't expect to beat her
just because you have a little help.

04:14.098 --> 04:17.957
Even if I phone it in, you'd just
barely have a fighting chance.

04:18.731 --> 04:21.911
All I can really help you
with is mental arithmetic,

04:22.135 --> 04:26.111
and jump rope, on the off chance
that one gets picked for real.

04:26.768 --> 04:31.809
Will you even be allowed to participate
while Sakayanagi is on high alert?

04:32.251 --> 04:37.563
There's only one other person in Class A
besides me who's any good at mental arithmetic.

04:38.617 --> 04:43.226
If she doesn't choose me for it,
just call it bad luck and give up.

04:44.867 --> 04:46.867
Let's go report this to Horikita.

04:47.007 --> 04:50.741
No, she'll just get mad at you
for going behind her back.

04:51.398 --> 04:53.922
Let me find the right timing to tell her.

04:55.211 --> 04:56.305
Got it.

05:06.673 --> 05:07.735
What is it?

05:08.040 --> 05:10.086
Would you mind coming over?

05:12.938 --> 05:15.914
I don't have a good feeling about this.

05:24.043 --> 05:27.814
Barley miso? I didn't know you could cook.

05:27.971 --> 05:30.541
It's nothing to boast about, really.

05:31.026 --> 05:34.135
Anyway, I assume you've already eaten.

05:35.889 --> 05:38.233
Let's get to the matter at hand, shall we?

05:39.075 --> 05:42.091
I'll just say thanks for the food this time.

05:42.669 --> 05:44.654
This isn't really working for you.

05:45.115 --> 05:47.982
You're right. I'll think of something else.

05:48.092 --> 05:50.951
No, that's not what I meant.

05:52.896 --> 05:57.641
I've thought about what would be the most
beneficial plan for our class in the exam.

05:58.533 --> 06:00.784
I'd like to get your feedback.

06:05.461 --> 06:08.648
This much data paints a clear
picture of the whole class.

06:08.930 --> 06:13.547
I've agonized over everything
all week to come up with this.

06:14.446 --> 06:19.228
I have no objections to this.
But I'd like to make one request.

06:19.501 --> 06:20.297
What is it?

06:20.638 --> 06:24.954
If Class A's chess event comes up,
I want you to do it.

06:25.314 --> 06:26.422
Me?

06:27.103 --> 06:30.547
I suppose we will need someone
to prepare for it, but…

06:30.868 --> 06:31.891
Why me?

06:32.696 --> 06:35.868
I think you're the best person for me to teach.

06:36.454 --> 06:39.946
Very well. In that case, how shall we practice?

06:40.431 --> 06:43.251
We can do it online, late at night.

06:43.782 --> 06:46.235
That would prevent anyone from finding out.

06:48.579 --> 06:50.751
Do you think we can beat Class A?

06:51.376 --> 06:54.566
I don't see them as undefeatable.

06:54.652 --> 06:57.042
That's my conclusion, looking at this data.

06:58.814 --> 07:01.032
I'll leave the rest to you.

07:04.290 --> 07:05.266
That just leaves…

07:10.431 --> 07:12.111
Wait a moment, Hirata.

07:13.047 --> 07:15.063
I just want to make one thing clear.

07:16.032 --> 07:19.610
On the day of the exam,
I don't plan for you to participate.

07:20.306 --> 07:24.446
However, if we end up needing extra participants,

07:24.688 --> 07:26.828
will you at least do the bare minimum?

07:29.063 --> 07:31.063
So you won't give me an answer.

07:35.618 --> 07:38.032
I don't think… we can win this.

07:38.110 --> 07:40.110
Not with Hirata in this state.

07:40.220 --> 07:42.696
We don't have much time until the exam.

07:44.735 --> 07:46.383
Hirata, wait up!

07:46.907 --> 07:51.750
Please, Hirata, we really need your help.

07:51.907 --> 07:52.841
Will you…

07:53.404 --> 07:56.396
You still can't leave me alone?

07:56.865 --> 07:58.670
Of course I can't.

07:58.733 --> 08:01.443
Can you get Yamauchi back, then?

08:01.522 --> 08:02.399
Huh?

08:02.966 --> 08:06.888
Talking to you is a waste of time. I'm leaving.

08:16.658 --> 08:18.275
Ouch…

08:18.548 --> 08:20.837
If you keep following me around, I'll…

08:20.923 --> 08:22.400
What have we here?

08:22.892 --> 08:25.821
Still acting the coward?

08:26.267 --> 08:28.814
We've already seen your ugly side.

08:29.931 --> 08:33.054
Oh, don't mind me.

08:33.361 --> 08:35.416
Carry on with what you were doing.

08:35.945 --> 08:37.049
Do you…

08:37.467 --> 08:39.484
want something from me?

08:39.828 --> 08:44.367
I'm the man who has everything.
If there's anything you can do for me,

08:44.664 --> 08:47.468
just stay out of my sight, would you?

08:48.234 --> 08:51.745
You've got some nerve. You have
no idea what I'm going through.

08:51.941 --> 08:54.972
I don't, nor do I care to find out.

08:55.152 --> 08:57.579
T-That's enough, Kouenji!

08:57.739 --> 09:00.192
Hirata isn't doing anything wrong.

09:00.434 --> 09:02.121
My apologies.

09:02.473 --> 09:07.113
But the sooner you forget about
my boy Hirata here, the better.

09:07.887 --> 09:09.941
He's a lost cause.

09:13.512 --> 09:16.332
I'm already at rock bottom, Kouenji!

09:21.325 --> 09:24.989
If you want a fight, I'll show you no mercy.

09:27.025 --> 09:32.030
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

09:35.133 --> 09:39.258
If you're done with her, why don't I
take her off your hands?

09:46.854 --> 09:48.137
L-Let go of me!

09:48.162 --> 09:49.849
I'm afraid I can't do that.

09:50.123 --> 09:53.802
Your heart is broken, and now you're injured, too.

09:54.060 --> 09:56.365
Let me take care of you now.

09:56.639 --> 10:00.433
I, um…! I'm actually not injured at all!

10:00.842 --> 10:02.896
Now, now, not to worry.

10:03.162 --> 10:06.189
I'm much more gentle than I look.

10:06.811 --> 10:09.248
Let go! Put me down!

10:10.151 --> 10:11.694
I simply couldn't.

10:11.941 --> 10:15.261
Not when I've already gotten my hands on you.

10:15.527 --> 10:16.950
Huh?!

10:20.082 --> 10:22.441
You still haven't had enough of me?

10:23.485 --> 10:26.477
This is how you're going to try to hurt me?

10:26.759 --> 10:28.165
Not at all.

10:28.501 --> 10:31.180
You're the one hurting everyone around you.

10:33.658 --> 10:35.545
Say what you will about me,

10:35.569 --> 10:39.400
but I wouldn't belittle a girl who's
only trying to show me kindness.

10:41.994 --> 10:44.048
Get out of my sight, would you?

10:53.081 --> 10:54.503
Hirata…

10:55.315 --> 10:58.470
That's enough chasing after him for today.

11:17.722 --> 11:18.706
Hirata.

11:20.300 --> 11:22.143
One after another…

11:22.175 --> 11:24.237
Why is everyone coming after me?

11:24.698 --> 11:28.159
Are you going to shove me away
and leave like you did with Mii?

11:29.488 --> 11:33.651
I'm too tired to muster up
the energy for that now.

11:34.441 --> 11:37.073
So, is there something you wanted to say?

11:37.574 --> 11:39.987
I'd rather you do the talking.

11:42.605 --> 11:45.464
You've been dwelling on Yamauchi's expulsion,

11:45.683 --> 11:47.995
and making no effort to help the class.

11:49.019 --> 11:54.300
What I want to know is what made you
see things the way you do.

11:55.511 --> 12:00.042
What good would it do you
to know that, even if I did tell you?

12:00.542 --> 12:01.643
Just tell me.

12:05.179 --> 12:10.241
There's something dark in your eyes
that scares me sometimes.

12:14.343 --> 12:17.139
It started when I was in middle school.

12:18.546 --> 12:22.608
I had this close friend who was being bullied.

12:23.632 --> 12:25.928
I wanted to help him.

12:26.851 --> 12:30.983
But I was scared of getting bullied myself,

12:31.507 --> 12:33.507
so I ended up just standing by.

12:34.241 --> 12:35.928
And then, one day…

12:36.585 --> 12:39.590
that friend tried to jump to his death.

12:47.194 --> 12:49.194
He just barely survived,

12:49.764 --> 12:53.951
but he hasn't recovered. He's still in a coma.

12:55.364 --> 13:00.152
He decided to take his own life
because of something I did.

13:00.946 --> 13:03.383
It's not entirely your fault.

13:05.986 --> 13:10.712
I know. But I didn't intervene, so I'm complicit.

13:11.330 --> 13:16.032
I thought my friend's attempt would put
an end to this whole series of problems.

13:16.700 --> 13:18.121
But I was wrong.

13:18.286 --> 13:22.856
After it happened, I saw the
boundless darkness of humanity.

13:24.155 --> 13:27.772
The bullies just found a new classmate to target.

13:29.488 --> 13:31.488
I couldn't believe it.

13:32.449 --> 13:35.300
Some kid who had never gotten involved

13:35.550 --> 13:37.410
had to go through the same thing.

13:37.770 --> 13:44.629
Even classmates who hadn't participated in
the bullying before were starting to join in.

13:46.070 --> 13:48.476
With the kid in the lowest caste gone,

13:48.851 --> 13:53.210
the next one from the bottom became the lowest.

13:53.531 --> 13:55.703
You could say that's the natural order.

13:57.040 --> 13:59.821
I knew I had to stop it.

14:00.399 --> 14:01.524
So…

14:02.016 --> 14:04.367
I began my reign of terror.

14:05.141 --> 14:06.399
You?

14:07.243 --> 14:09.500
I didn't pull any punches.

14:10.766 --> 14:13.227
There was no one who could stand up to me.

14:14.001 --> 14:18.953
I stood alone above everyone,
leaving them all at the bottom.

14:20.001 --> 14:24.977
If anyone picked a fight, I'd make both sides
suffer the same pain and punishment.

14:28.157 --> 14:32.141
I must have ruined that entire
year of school, after all that.

14:33.204 --> 14:35.516
They all stopped smiling,

14:35.844 --> 14:39.527
and went on living cold and detached, like robots.

14:40.441 --> 14:46.394
So that's why you couldn't stand the rest
of the class singling out Yamauchi.

14:48.637 --> 14:52.137
In the end, I still couldn't save him.

14:52.754 --> 14:57.081
I should have known I wasn't
cut out to bring the class together.

14:57.707 --> 15:01.863
I almost started a reign of terror
to protect someone again.

15:02.574 --> 15:07.120
It's not Horikita's fault that
Yamauchi got expelled,

15:07.167 --> 15:09.449
and I can't claim responsibility, either.

15:09.746 --> 15:11.683
Do you understand that?

15:12.238 --> 15:14.917
Yeah. It was a lost cause.

15:16.031 --> 15:19.171
There was nothing any of us could have done.

15:19.539 --> 15:21.226
You're wrong.

15:23.044 --> 15:26.050
The one responsible for Yamauchi's expulsion…

15:27.364 --> 15:28.833
is you, Hirata.

15:31.216 --> 15:33.489
If you wanted to save him,

15:33.864 --> 15:36.895
it was up to you to do that, no matter the cost.

15:37.497 --> 15:40.286
But I… I tried, as hard as I could!

15:40.395 --> 15:42.434
And I still couldn't do anything!

15:42.731 --> 15:47.422
Ichinose kept everyone in Class B
off the chopping block.

15:48.039 --> 15:52.586
Yeah, but… she's a special case.

15:52.992 --> 15:56.422
She could only do that because
she has so many private points!

15:56.954 --> 16:01.516
Then the problem is that you haven't
been leading the same way she has.

16:01.625 --> 16:03.625
You're not being fair!

16:04.055 --> 16:06.461
Sure. But the fact remains,

16:06.672 --> 16:08.976
you chose this path yourself.

16:09.313 --> 16:11.832
You have this fantasy of saving everyone,

16:11.994 --> 16:15.078
but you just end up burying it inside.

16:16.250 --> 16:19.351
But if this is still how you feel,

16:19.546 --> 16:22.749
it's your responsibility when you fail.

16:23.118 --> 16:25.180
You need to be prepared for that.

16:25.789 --> 16:26.648
But, I…!

16:26.743 --> 16:28.687
I was wrong.

16:29.500 --> 16:35.391
I came to think of you as a principled person who
commanded most of your classmates' respect.

16:35.586 --> 16:37.180
But you're not.

16:37.438 --> 16:42.851
You're just some incompetent student who
talks big, but can't actually do anything.

16:44.250 --> 16:47.726
That's who you really are, Hirata Yousuke.

16:50.984 --> 16:53.195
How long can you keep living a fantasy?

16:54.508 --> 16:57.734
Is this… what you're really like?

16:58.507 --> 17:02.100
Frightening, unforgiving,
speaking only cold words…

17:03.351 --> 17:05.849
You can dream all you want.

17:06.382 --> 17:08.632
But if you really want to save everyone,

17:08.741 --> 17:14.171
the only way you can do it is by
fighting tooth and nail to the bitter end.

17:15.342 --> 17:19.796
If someone gets expelled along the way,
you have to suck it up and deal with it.

17:20.028 --> 17:22.520
All you can do is to keep moving forward.

17:23.957 --> 17:26.005
That's so bleak.

17:26.857 --> 17:32.091
If you give up now, you're going to
lose more and more people.

17:32.646 --> 17:36.997
That's reason enough for you to
keep your head up and keep going.

17:37.466 --> 17:43.684
That way, you'll still have plenty of people
standing behind you in the end.

17:44.974 --> 17:50.833
I have to just push through it all by myself?

17:51.700 --> 17:55.426
When am I ever allowed to not be okay?

17:55.927 --> 18:00.349
When you need it, you can let
the rest of the class support you.

18:01.279 --> 18:05.075
When you're not okay,
lean on someone you can trust.

18:05.990 --> 18:08.833
Don't worry about the past or the future.

18:09.591 --> 18:12.591
But, I… don't know if…

18:13.373 --> 18:16.255
I can still lead everyone, at this point.

18:19.240 --> 18:23.333
You're better suited to lead as you are now.

18:25.091 --> 18:26.169
Thank you…

18:26.912 --> 18:29.239
Thank you, Ayanokouji…

18:35.068 --> 18:36.169
That should do it.

18:51.710 --> 18:54.412
G-Good morning, Hirata…

18:55.554 --> 18:56.616
Good morning.

18:57.780 --> 18:59.139
Sorry about yesterday.

19:00.335 --> 19:02.897
I was really mean to you, Mii.

19:03.444 --> 19:07.787
I'm sorry for ignoring you when
you kept trying to reach out to me, too.

19:08.022 --> 19:13.530
N-No, you don't have to, I…

19:14.413 --> 19:15.733
Good morning, everyone!

19:15.983 --> 19:17.905
H-Hirata?

19:18.423 --> 19:20.423
And, I'm sorry!

19:21.728 --> 19:24.173
I know it's a little late for apologies…

19:25.204 --> 19:29.970
But if it's okay with all of you, I'd like to
start doing my part for the class again.

19:30.416 --> 19:31.821
Hirata!

19:31.970 --> 19:33.204
What happened to you?

19:33.587 --> 19:34.657
It's about time.

19:34.697 --> 19:35.485
Yeah!

19:36.854 --> 19:38.158
What happened?

19:39.604 --> 19:41.104
Good morning, Horikita.

19:41.557 --> 19:43.689
Y-Yes, good morning.

19:44.104 --> 19:48.970
I don't think I was wrong during the class voting.

19:50.002 --> 19:50.853
I see.

19:51.330 --> 19:54.705
But you weren't in the wrong, either.

19:55.299 --> 19:58.064
Actually, it was the only right move.

19:58.777 --> 20:01.855
You've changed your tune
quite a bit since yesterday.

20:02.355 --> 20:06.261
I'm going to do everything I can
to earn back the trust I lost.

20:21.995 --> 20:23.276
Checkmate.

20:24.933 --> 20:26.409
I need more practice.

20:26.457 --> 20:31.589
You've gotten pretty good at chess
over a really short period of time.

20:32.362 --> 20:35.901
But even when you go easy on me,
I almost always lose.

20:36.449 --> 20:40.964
You won't be going up against anyone harder
than me when I'm going easy on you.

20:41.472 --> 20:43.519
You're awfully confident.

20:44.043 --> 20:46.487
Not really, just experienced.

20:47.074 --> 20:50.042
Let's pick this back up tomorrow.

20:50.425 --> 20:53.144
Alright. See you tomorrow.

20:53.660 --> 20:54.534
Yeah.

21:03.050 --> 21:07.139
[Final Special Exam]

22:37.418 --> 22:40.030
[Final Special Exam
Leader Meeting Point]

22:40.145 --> 22:42.308
Kaneda is late.

22:51.785 --> 22:53.207
Ryuuen?

22:53.707 --> 22:55.210
What are you doing here?

22:56.614 --> 22:58.710
What are you freaked out for?

22:58.863 --> 23:00.406
I see how it is.

23:00.867 --> 23:06.969
You must have assumed that the person with
the protection point would be the leader.

23:07.549 --> 23:13.720
But if the one with the protection point
can't do it, someone else has to step in.

23:13.830 --> 23:14.930
Don't you think?

23:15.268 --> 23:17.064
You've got me there.

23:17.158 --> 23:21.158
So this is Ryuuen's last stand,
without a protection point.

23:21.736 --> 23:25.267
In any case, it's bound to be
a fascinating showdown.

23:26.158 --> 23:29.705
Well, it seems we're all here.

23:29.955 --> 23:31.531
Shall we begin?
